  {
    "episode_id": 83221,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83221.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 3,
    "turn_text": "President Joe Biden is sticking with his plan to have all American troops and citizens out of Afghanistan by the August 31 deadline. Biden met virtually with G7 leaders Tuesday morning. It is reported that seven nations represented at the meeting were prepared to extend the August 31st deadline against the demands of the Taliban. Biden said America would stick to the plan and be out by August 31st, providing the Taliban cooperates with the current evacuation. The Heritage Foundation's Vice President for Foreign Policy and National Security James Carofano joined Fox Business Tuesday to discuss the August 31st deadline.",
