      },
      {
        "text": "The Taliban lacks the capacity or willingness to control the situation independently after the US departure.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "People currently unable to reach the airport will remain unable despite efforts to improve access.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Reversing a military withdrawal once underway requires intact logistical infrastructure and operational capability.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "A large-scale abandonment of civilians constitutes a moral failure for the US.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "The Taliban’s potential actions against the evacuation process are credible threats rather than mere posturing.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "There is a clear distinction between 'withdrawing' and 'abandoning', and the former carries ethical weight.",
        "confidence": 0.86
      },
      {
        "text": "The evacuation timeline must account for real-time mobility constraints of civilians under threat.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      },
      {
        "text": "The US bears responsibility for ensuring safe passage for evacuees regardless of external actors’ behavior.",
        "confidence": 0.84
      },
      {
        "text": "The consequences of failing to evacuate people outweigh the political costs of prolonged presence.",
        "confidence": 0.83
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
