    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83221.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 33,
    "turn_text": "Well, this is what we have to get to the bottom of. And I'm sure there will be many inquiries following this episode. The thing that we need to focus on right now is evacuating as many people as possible. First, American citizens and those special immigrant, visa holders, we need to get them out. But yes, this is a question we need to know and understand. Did President Biden simply ignore the warnings that were coming from the intelligence community? Did he heed the warnings that were coming from the Department of Defense? Did they underestimate the Taliban and the Taliban strength? I think these are all things that we need to know and understand. But that will be secondary right now. We'll have to figure that out. The first priority really needs to be focusing on Americans and making sure that they can get to safety. But in my estimation, having served in the military for over 23 years, we should always have those plans in place. Number one, evacuating Americans. Number two, destroying our military equipment so that it can't fall into the hands of the Taliban. Number three is getting our troops out. And number four, of course, is destroying those air bases or other bases that existed. So they can't be used by the Taliban and the other violent extremist organizations. I think this is all very basic. And this administration, they knew better or they should have known better. But here we are today with those horrible images of a humanitarian crisis on the rise in Afghanistan.",
